.TH LINUX-DISTRO-MATRIX 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware M8.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-distro-matrix \- read-only Linux distribution acceptance evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-distro-matrix
.RB [ --mode " offline|host|container" ]
.RB [ --format " tsv|jsonl" ]
.RB [ --target " debian|ubuntu|arch|almalinux|rocky" ]...
.RB [ --require-complete ]
.RB [ --engine " docker|podman" ]
.RB [ --image " distro=repository@sha256:HEX" ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports only identity-level evidence. Offline mode exercises synthetic
os-release fixtures and makes no claim about running systems. Host mode checks
the actual Linux distribution. Container mode requires an explicit engine and
pre-cached digest-pinned images with Perl; it does not pull images or install
packages. Native firewall and host security policy tests are outside scope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --mode offline|host|container
Choose fixture, host or explicit container evidence. Default is offline.
.TP
.B --format tsv|jsonl
Choose tab-separated seven-field output or schema-versioned JSON Lines.
.TP
.BI --target " DISTRO"
Filter to one or more supported distributions. Default: all five.
.TP
.B --require-complete
Return nonzero when any target was SKIP, even when there is no FAIL.
.TP
.BI --engine " docker|podman"
Required only for container mode. The executable is selected from fixed paths.
.TP
.BI --image " DISTRO=REPO@sha256:DIGEST"
Provide a pre-cached immutable image reference. Repeat per target.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show tool version.
.SH OUTPUT
TARGET, MODE, STATUS, OBSERVED_ID, FAMILY, EVIDENCE, REASON.
PASS implies an exact ID match. SKIP is not a passing platform acceptance.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No failed checks; may still include SKIP without --require-complete.
.TP
.B 1
At least one attempted check failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.TP
.B 4
Incomplete coverage (SKIP) when --require-complete was requested.
.SH SECURITY
No shell interpolation of user-supplied paths or images. Containers run with
network disabled, no extra capabilities, no new privileges, a read-only root
and repository mount, unprivileged UID, and bounded resources. Evaluate images
and container daemon privileges separately; prefer isolated VMs for
untrusted images and native firewall acceptance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linux-platform-report (1)
